KZ3 patch 4026 (network pass 43): keyboard and mouse count as their own controller, so split-screen co-op needs one pad
only. Before, patch 2037 OR'ed the keys into port 0, so one pad + keyboard was one controller and the
co-op gate (numactivecontrollers < 2 -> dlg_controlerror) refused.

New libs/input/pad_kbport.h (platform-free; host test tools/net/test_kb_port.c): the game's player-per-slot table
(1.14 Game 0x015FCF80 + 0x9C + i * 0x90, 1.00 0x01587880 + 0x94 + i * 0x90; the EBOOT checked by two code words of
the assignment function 0x004D5ED0 / 1.00 0x004C8FD4) and the route: while a host pad is connected, the keyboard is
reported as one more connected controller on the first port without a pad; its keys go to that port alone once the
game has given that slot a player (the co-op player 2), else into the port of the game's player 1 (single player and
menus keep pad + keyboard on one player, as before). No pad, an unknown EBOOT or KZ3_KB_OWN_PORT=0: as before.
Logs "[kbport] ..." once per change (route, the game's players by slot, the slots it sees connected).
Test input: KZ3_TEST_FAKE_PAD=1 (port 0 counts as a host pad), KZ3_KB_SCRIPT / KZ3_KB_SCRIPT_FILE (PAD_SCRIPT's
grammar and clock, pressed as keyboard input). KZ3-specific (the game's table); the idea of a keyboard port next to
the pads is general.

